macarons chocolate bonbons fresh  strawberries and cream but the catches  they're all fake i may and i'm a faux  food artist  the most popular item in my shop is  definitely macarons i start off by  kneading the clay adding spritz of water  i'll spread the clay with a rolling pin  i then cut them into halves so i can  feed them into a clay maker i started  creating fake food four years ago when i  used to work at a bag and the artist in  me was hungry for creation  i'm a lover of food and crafts so fake  food was a common denominator i knew i  needed to turn this hobby into a  business when my tennessee dining table  was covered with cupcakes  i get my inspirations from the japanese  baked food culture and memories of  patisserie shops in france where  desserts decorated the displays like  high-end fashion  because there isn't a textbook how to  make fake food the challenge is to  search for materials and methods on my  own  i think each fake food artist keeps  their methods secret so  i gather hints from crap videos and  blogs  it's rewarding when you finally find a  way to make something out of nothing  after the paint dries i use a glue gun  to add the filling  here i'm using white for vanilla  i also have milk chocolate dark  chocolate and caramel fillings  meringue peaks are one of my favorites  to make  real or fake the key to a perfect  barangay is to achieve a light airy  softness and to get those signature  peaks  first i turn the clay into small pieces  this will allow the clay to soak the  water faster  i add glue and mix until getting a silky  consistency with a rubber spatula this  will help create the peaks  then i use a hand mixer until i get a  smooth fine mirroring a texture  i pipe the clay through a star tip onto  a baking sheet  two to three days later when dry i add  the finishing touches  today i'm dipping them into chocolate  and adding sprinkles of course i'll fake  i think strawberries are the hardest but  most rewarding to make they add a pop of  color and look beautiful on cakes  once i prepped the clay i measured them  into about .4 ounce pieces and yes i  have strawberry sizes small to large  with a set weight i then place the clay  on a flower nail and mold it into a  strawberry shape  then i add the seeds using a needle tip  shaped like a teardrop  the clay is soft so i need to be very  careful not to lose the strawberry shape  after three to four days the  strawberries are ready for painting  for finishing touches i will add gloss  for that perfect shiny juicy look  now the fun part for today  i'm going to be making the alphabet tea  for tasty  i start off painting the two wood panels  brown to make chocolate cookies  i glue on wood pieces that will hold the  two layers in place  then i start to outline the cake with  thick cream using a round piping tip  once that is finished i place the top  cookie layer  then to support the farm i drive screws  in with a power drill  now the movement that we're all waiting  for it's time to decorate i prep the  surface with glue so the clay will have  a strong bond  i covered a cookie with generous amounts  of cream  assembling is like a painting process  choosing a color thinking of a theme  a message  today i wanted to express the fun  vibrant and whimsy that tasty brings to  food  i feel our love for sweets is a  universal language  it's like celebrating that special  occasion surrounding a cake with loved  ones  and voila  we have our fake cookie cake  i hope you had fun watching and getting  a little glimpse into the world of fake  food happy april fool's day  oh yes  you
 

